    "All action-based triggers and archival/live scores pass boundary tests, including freeze across tricks and reroll rescue without manufactured initial failure.",
    "Bonus frequencies differ substantially; this is not a direct player fairness measure because all players face the same module. Prepared scenarios show every goal is achievable.",
    "The ending-Epic goal is highly dependent on draft and play preparation. Ordinary controllers almost never achieve it; its rarity cannot be treated as a pure dice probability. Controlled Hurricane/Ollie ordering confirms a much lower banked rate when the four-die Epic must come last.",
    "At the same diverse module settings, four-die premium +4 favors the prepared four-die profile more than premium +2. Retain +2 as the candidate for human tests.",
    "Double Quai needs a focused human test or a separately tested easing to one pair; its current natural frequency should not be mistaken for a broken trigger. Candidate changes remain recommendations, not simulated replacement rules.",
